// A bare lambda that ends a body is read as the box that the body returns
// only where the expected type returns a box of a function. Two cases keep
// their `return`, and each is refused here. A box of a computation that is
// no function has no lambda to read, so the lambda is refused with
// `ShapeMismatch`. A definition that states no type gives no box to read
// against, so its lambda is refused with `NotSynthesisable`.
//
// - see: #6390

/// Two values.
data Two : Type where
  /// The left value.
  | Left : Two
  /// The right value.
  | Right : Two

/// A box of a computation that is no function.
@[refuses("ShapeMismatch")]
def no_function() -> +U (-F Two) =
  fun (u) {
    return u
  }

/// No type is stated.
@[refuses("NotSynthesisable")]
def unstated = fun (u) { return u };
